Sval: the update-in-progress question asks what its buttons answer

Leaving automatic updates while one downloads asks whether to continue,
and answers with Discard and Continue, which do not say what each does to
the update. The question asks whether to finish the download, says the
new setting applies after it, and the buttons name the update.

diff --git a/browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/preferences.ftl b/browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/preferences.ftl
index d2fbb42f7d..c8871a2445 100644
--- a/browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/preferences.ftl
+++ b/browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/preferences.ftl
@@ -810,14 +810,14 @@ update-setting-write-failure-message2 =
 
     Could not write to file: { $path }
 
-update-in-progress-title = Update In Progress
+update-in-progress-title = Finish the update that’s downloading?
 
-update-in-progress-message = Do you want { -brand-short-name } to continue with this update?
+update-in-progress-message = Your new setting applies to the updates after this one.
 
-update-in-progress-ok-button = &Discard
+update-in-progress-ok-button = &Discard Update
 # Continue is the cancel button so pressing escape or using a platform standard
 # method of closing the UI will not discard the update.
-update-in-progress-cancel-button = &Continue
+update-in-progress-cancel-button = &Finish Update
 
 ## Firefox support
 
